+     timers count.  The CPU runs from the main clock divided as CM0/CM1 say;
+     this firmware sets CM1 = 0x40, divide by two, so the CPU runs at
+     3.6864 MHz against the timers' 7.3728.  The cycle counts themselves are
+     the software manual's, per instruction (see m32c_insn_cpu_cycles); an
+     instruction without one is charged M32C_CPI f1 cycles, the old flat
+     estimate.  An interrupt accepted after the last instruction adds its
+     interrupt sequence, 18 cycles (software manual table 5.3.1).  */
