+	      /* Raise the request; the controller below decides when to take
+		 it.  0x005D is what re-triggers vector 29, whose handler is the
+		 firmware's main loop -- without this the loop runs once and
+		 stops.  Whether TB2 is really vector 29's source is the open
+		 question in notes.md; M32C_TB2_VECTOR=0 disables it.  */
